metadata.description:
{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Phase Rotation (RX-style)} - a REAPER re-creation of the iZotope RX "Phase" module for media items.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Suggest finds the channel-linked fixed rotation that minimises the peak level of the selected items; Left/Right rotation sliders with Link; Adaptive phase rotation; Preview / Bypass; Render bakes the rotation into a new take. Processing is done by the bundled JSFX "Phase Rotation (RX-style, Hilbert)" (linear-phase FIR Hilbert transformer, 0 degrees = bit-transparent), inserted as a take FX so everything stays non-destructive until you press Render.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Select one or more audio items and run the action. Keys: S = Suggest, Space = Preview, B = Bypass, Esc = close.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b reaper_phaserot} applies broadband phase rotation to a media item's SOURCE: playback, render and the waveform display all show the rotated audio, no files are written, no take FX is added, and the project file stays a plain project (without the extension the original file plays unprocessed). Used by the script "Phase Rotation (RX-style)"; also exposes the ReaScript API PhaseRot_SetTake / PhaseRot_ClearTake / PhaseRot_GetTake / PhaseRot_Analyze.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Restart REAPER after installing.\par}
}
